From: Alexander Theißen <alex@theissen.io>
Subject: [PATCH] winemac: Don't double HORZRES and VERTRES in retina mode.

Ported for CrossOver 26.3 from athei/wine commit
6a52255e56a56e7366d5013075d2ce81149fa624, code unchanged; the same
change is Highball's patch 0020. A downstream fix, not a WineHQ
backport: WineHQ still doubles both caps through wine-11.20.

macdrv_GetDeviceCaps doubled both caps whenever retina mode was on,
on top of the fallback implementation. That fallback now returns the
primary monitor rect or SM_CXSCREEN/SM_CYSCREEN, and winemac already
reports monitors in pixels in retina mode (a882106e38), so a retina
process saw HORZRES twice the width that EnumDisplaySettings,
GetSystemMetrics and DESKTOPHORZRES report: 6048 against 3024 on a
3024x1964 panel for a DPI-aware process, and 3024 against an
SM_CXSCREEN of 1512 for an unaware one.

Programs that size or centre windows from HORZRES and VERTRES place
them on a desktop twice the real size. Pass both caps through to the
fallback unchanged. Nothing changes unless RetinaMode is enabled.
---
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c
@@ -213,15 +213,10 @@ static INT macdrv_GetDeviceCaps(PHYSDEV dev, INT cap)
     case VERTSIZE:
         ret = vert_size;
         break;
-    case HORZRES:
-    case VERTRES:
     default:
         pthread_mutex_unlock(&device_data_mutex);
         dev = GET_NEXT_PHYSDEV( dev, pGetDeviceCaps );
-        ret = dev->funcs->pGetDeviceCaps( dev, cap );
-        if ((cap == HORZRES || cap == VERTRES) && retina_on)
-            ret *= 2;
-        return ret;
+        return dev->funcs->pGetDeviceCaps( dev, cap );
     }
 
     TRACE("cap %d -> %d\n", cap, ret);
